===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gewH-|*leyg-|id2=like}}
The {{glossary|adjective}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|comly}}, {{m|enm|comli}}, {{m|enm|cumly}}, {{m|enm|cumlich|t=of a person: beautiful, handsome, etc.; of noble birth, bearing, or character; of behaviour: appropriate, becoming; of an event: convenient; favourable; of a thing: beautiful, wonderful; fitting, proper}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=cǒmlī|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=MED8546}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|cymlīċ}}, {{m|ang|cȳmlīċ|t=beautiful, comely; splendid; convenient}}, from {{m|ang|cȳme|t=beautiful, comely; splendid; exquisite, fine}} + {{m|ang|-līċ|pos={{glossary|suffix}} meaning ‘like; relating to’ forming adjectives}}. {{m|ang||Cȳme}} is derived from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kūmiz|t=delicate; feeble}}, from {{m|en|gem-pro|*kūmalīkaz|t=dear; pitiful}}, probably related to {{m|gem-pro|*kūmaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*kūmijaz|t=pitiful; frail, weak}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gewH-|t=to call, name; to call on, invoke; to cry, cry out}}. The word was influenced by {{m|en|come|pos=verb}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=1764049049|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref>

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the adjective.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=2444655492|date=September 2023}}</ref>

