# {{lb|en|dated|or|archaic}}
## Of a [[person#Noun|person]]: [[attractive]] or [[pleasing#Adjective|pleasing]] to [[look at]]; [[beautiful#Adjective|beautiful]], [[handsome#Adjective|handsome]]; also, attractive but not [[particularly]] beautiful or handsome.
##: {{synonyms|en|pulchritudinous|Thesaurus:beautiful}}
##: {{antonyms|en|homely|uncomely|Thesaurus:ugly}}
##: {{ux|en|a '''comely''' woman}}
##* {{RQ:Milton Comus|page=3|passage=Not once perceive their foul disfigurement, / But boaſt themſelves more '''comely''' than before}}
##* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|volume=I|chapter=A Sermon Preached at the Cathedral-Church of St. Paul’s, November the 9th, 1662 [Julian calendar]|date=9 November 1662|page=55|passage=He that is '''comely''', when old and decrepit, ſurely was very beautiful, when he was young.}}
##* {{RQ:Prior Solomon|page=448|passage=Then had I come, preventing {{smallcaps|Sheba}}'s Queen, / To ſee the '''comelieſt''' of the Sons of Men; {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Wilde Dorian Gray|chapter=I|page=2|passage=As the painter looked at the gracious and '''comely''' form he had so skilfully mirrored in his art, a smile of pleasure passed across his face, and seemed about to linger there.}}
##* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot|chapter=IX|passage=The chief's name was To-jo, and his household consisted of seven females and himself. These women were much more '''comely''', or rather less hideous than those of Tsa's people; one of them, even, was almost pretty, being less hairy and having a rather nice skin, with high coloring.}}
## Of a person, an [[action#Noun|action]], [[behavior|behaviour]], etc.: [[meet#Verb|meeting]] [[accepted#Adjective|accepted]] [[moral#Adjective|moral]] or [[social#Adjective|social]] [[norm#Noun|norms]]; [[appropriate#Adjective|appropriate]], [[becoming#Adjective|becoming]], [[proper#Adjective|proper]].
##: {{synonyms|en|agreeable|seemly|Thesaurus:suitable}}
##: {{antonyms|en|improper|inappropriate|unbecoming|uncomely|unseemly|Thesaurus:unsuitable}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|IV|vi|23|1|This is a happier and more '''comely''' time, / Then when these Fellowes ran about the streets, / Crying Confusion.}}
##* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|147|1|passage=Praise ye the Lord: for it is good to sing praises vnto our God: for it is pleasant, and praise is '''comely'''.}}
##* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|chapter=Charity, Composed of All Three Kindes, Pleasant, Profitable, Honest|partition=3|section=1|member=3|page=527|passage=Behold hovv '''comely''' and good a thing it is for brethren to liue together in vnion: {{...}}|footer=From [[w:Psalms|Psalm]] 133:1 of the [[Bible]].}}
## Of a [[thing]]: beautiful, [[elegant]], [[well#Adverb|well]]-[[compose]]d; also, [[delicate#Adjective|delicate]], [[fine#Adjective|fine]].
##: {{antonyms|en|uncomely}}
##* {{RQ:Ascham Works|title=Toxophilus|page=162|passage=In ſhootinge at the prickes, haſtye and quicke drawinge is neyther ſure nor yet '''comely'''.}}
